{"id":"23fee280935046f3bc03c4742ff7aa150c85687c","axis":"silent","repo":"codeigniter4/CodeIgniter4","sha":"23fee280935046f3bc03c4742ff7aa150c85687c","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/changelogs/v4.7.7.md","lines":["@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ Release Date: Unreleased"," - **HTTP:** Fixed a bug where `UploadedFile::move()` and `UploadedFile::store()` on Windows could store a file under a different name than `getName()` reported, or write its contents to an NTFS alternate data stream. Filenames ending in a period or space or containing a colon are now rejected, including explicitly supplied names."," - **Images:** Fixed a bug in `ImageMagickHandler::save()` where saving without an extension or with an unsupported extension threw an `ImagickException` instead of falling back to the image's format."," - **Security:** Fixed a bug where `Security::__construct()` threw a `TypeError` when the CSRF cookie was an array, causing an HTTP 500 response for affected requests.","+- **Security:** Fixed a bug in `strip_image_tags()` where an invalid PCRE character class caused attribute injection and improper quote handling, and ensured tags without `src` are stripped."," - **Session:** Fixed a bug where `BaseHandler::destroyCookie()` did not send the `SameSite` attribute in the `Set-Cookie` header, which could prevent browsers from properly clearing the session cookie."," - **Worker Mode:** Fixed a bug where every request that ended with an uncaught exception, including a `404 Page Not Found` without a 404 override, called `exit()` in the exception handler. This ended the worker script, so FrankenPHP booted a new one, and the worker loop skipped its cleanup after the request. The exception handler now returns to the worker loop."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/helpers/security_helper.md","lines":["@@ -44,7 +44,10 @@ For more info, please see the [Security Library](../libraries/security.md) docum"," "," - **Return type**: `string`"," ","-This is a security function that will strip image tags from a string. It leaves the image URL as plain text.","+This function replaces image tags with their `src` values and removes tags without `src`. It does not sanitize HTML or escape the returned values. Use appropriate escaping when displaying the result as text.","+","+!!! note \"Note\"","+    If tag replacement fails or the iteration limit is reached, any remaining `<img` prefixes are escaped as `&lt;img`, so the result may contain escaped tag text."," "," Example:"," "],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"system/Helpers/security_helper.php","lines":["@@ -85,18 +85,74 @@ function sanitize_filename(string $filename, bool $relativePath = false): string"," "," if (! function_exists('strip_image_tags')) {","     /**","-     * Strip Image Tags","+     * Replaces image tags with their raw src values.","+     *","+     * If tag replacement fails or the iteration limit is reached, remaining","+     * \"<img\" prefixes are escaped as \"&lt;img\".","+     *","+     * This function does not sanitize HTML. Escape the result appropriately","+     * when displaying it as text.","      */","     function strip_image_tags(string $str): string","     {","-        return preg_replace(","-            [","-                '#<img[\\s/]+.*?src\\s*=\\s*([\"\\'])([^\\\\1]+?)\\\\1.*?\\>#i',","-                '#<img[\\s/]+.*?src\\s*=\\s*?(([^\\s\"\\'=<>`]+)).*?\\>#i',","-            ],","-            '\\\\2',","-            $str,","-        );","+        if (! str_contains(strtolower($str), strtolower('<img'))) {","+            return $str;","+        }","+","+        // HTML whitespace excludes vertical tabs. Names may start with \"=\"","+        // and contain quotes; quoted values begin only after an assignment.","+        $whitespace = '[\\t\\n\\f\\r ]';","+        $separators = '[\\t\\n\\f\\r /]';","+        $name       = '[^\\t\\n\\f\\r />][^\\t\\n\\f\\r />=]*+';","+        $unquoted   = '[^\\t\\n\\f\\r >\"\\'][^\\t\\n\\f\\r >]*+';","+        $value      = '(?:\"[^\"]*+(?:\"|\\z)|\\'[^\\']*+(?:\\'|\\z)|' . $unquoted . ')';","+        $assignment = '(?:' . $whitespace . '*+=' . $whitespace . '*+(?:' . $value . ')?)?';","+        $attribute  = $name . $assignment;","+","+        $tagPattern = '#<img(?=[\\t\\n\\f\\r />]|\\z)((?:' . $separators . '++|' . $attribute . ')*+)(>|\\z)#i';","+","+        // Skip complete non-src attributes, then capture the first src value.","+        // Possessive repetition prevents searching inside earlier attributes.","+        $nameEnd    = '(?=[\\t\\n\\f\\r />=]|\\z)';","+        $srcPattern = '#\\A(?:' . $separators . '*+(?!src' . $nameEnd . ')' . $attribute . ')*+'","+            . $separators . '*+src' . $nameEnd","+            . '(?:' . $whitespace . '*+=' . $whitespace . '*+'","+            . '(?|\"([^\"]*+)\"|\\'([^\\']*+)\\'|(' . $unquoted . '))?)?#i';","+","+        $replace = static function (array $tag) use ($srcPattern): string {","+            // Browsers discard a tag that reaches EOF before its closing \">\".","+            if ($tag[2] === '') {","+                return '';","+            }","+","+            if (preg_match($srcPattern, $tag[1], $src) !== 1) {","+                return '';","+            }","+","+            return $src[1] ?? '';","+        };","+","+        // Removing a tag may join surrounding text into another image tag.","+        for ($remaining = 10; $remaining > 0; $remaining--) {","+            $result = preg_replace_callback($tagPattern, $replace, $str);","+","+            if ($result === null) {","+                break;","+            }","+","+            if ($result === $str) {","+                return $result;","+            }","+","+            $str = $result;","+","+            if ($remaining > 1 && ! str_contains(strtolower($str), strtolower('<img'))) {","+                return $str;","+            }","+        }","+","+        // Tag replacement failed or the iteration limit was reached.","+        return str_ireplace('<img', '&lt;img', $str);","     }"," }"," "],"additions":65,"deletions":9,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/system/Helpers/SecurityHelperTest.php","lines":["@@ -208,6 +208,122 @@ public function testStripImageTags(): void","         $this->assertSame('http://example.com/spacer.gif', strip_image_tags('http://example.com/spacer.gif'));"," ","         $this->assertSame('http://example.com/spacer.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"http://example.com/spacer.gif\" alt=\"Who needs CSS when you have a spacer.gif?\" />'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/spacer.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src=\\'http://example.com/spacer.gif\\' alt=\"test\" />'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/spacer.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src=http://example.com/spacer.gif alt=\"test\" />'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/spacer.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src  =  \"http://example.com/spacer.gif\" />'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/test.png', strip_image_tags('<img class=\"my-class\" id=\"my-img\" src=\"http://example.com/test.png\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/test.jpg', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\"test\\'s photo\" src=\"http://example.com/test.jpg\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/test.jpg', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\\'test \"quoted\" photo\\' src=\\'http://example.com/test.jpg\\'>'));","+","+        // Empty src or tags without src should be stripped","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"\" onerror=\"alert(1)\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img src=\\'\\' onerror=\\'alert(1)\\'>'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img onerror=\"alert(1)\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\"no image\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('Hello  World', strip_image_tags('Hello <img> World'));","+        $this->assertSame('Hello  World', strip_image_tags('Hello <img/> World'));","+        $this->assertSame('Hello  World', strip_image_tags('Hello <img > World'));","+","+        // Multiline img tag","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/test.png', strip_image_tags(\"<img\\n  class=\\\"foo\\\"\\n  src=\\\"http://example.com/test.png\\\"\\n  alt=\\\"bar\\\">\"));","+","+        // Intervening text between multiple img tags must not be swallowed","+        $this->assertSame('Text1  Text2 bar.jpg Text3', strip_image_tags('Text1 <img alt=\"foo\"> Text2 <img src=\"bar.jpg\"> Text3'));","+        $this->assertSame('Start 1.jpg Middle 2.jpg End', strip_image_tags('Start <img src=\"1.jpg\"> Middle <img src=\"2.jpg\"> End'));","+","+        // Attribute injection and quote handling","+        $this->assertSame('test', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"test\" onmouseover=\"alert(1)\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('test', strip_image_tags('<img src=\\'test\\' onmouseover=\\'alert(1)\\'>'));","+        $this->assertSame('test', strip_image_tags('<img src=\\'test\\' onmouseover=\"alert(1)\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('test', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"test\" onmouseover=\\'alert(1)\\'>'));","+","+        // Nested img tag bypass","+        $this->assertSame('x', strip_image_tags('<im<img>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+        $this->assertSame('x', strip_image_tags('<im<im<img>g>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+","+        // Only actual src attribute should be matched, not attributes ending with src (e.g. data-src)","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img data-src=\"http://example.com/fake.gif\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/real.gif', strip_image_tags('<img data-src=\"http://example.com/fake.gif\" src=\"http://example.com/real.gif\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('http://example.com/real.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"http://example.com/real.gif\" data-src=\"http://example.com/fake.gif\">'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsGreaterThanSignInsideQuotedAttribute(): void","+    {","+        $this->assertSame('photo.jpg', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\"><svg onload=alert(1)>\" src=\"photo.jpg\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('photo.jpg', strip_image_tags(\"<img alt='><svg onload=alert(1)>' src='photo.jpg'>\"));","+        $this->assertSame('photo.jpg', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"photo.jpg\" alt=\"><svg onload=alert(1)>\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\"><svg onload=alert(1)>\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('Before photo.jpg After', strip_image_tags('Before <img alt=\"a>b\" src=\"photo.jpg\"> After'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsNestedTags(): void","+    {","+        $this->assertSame('x', strip_image_tags('<im<img>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+        $this->assertSame('x', strip_image_tags('<im<im<img>g>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+        $this->assertStringNotContainsString('<img', strip_image_tags('<im<img>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+        $this->assertStringNotContainsString('onerror', strip_image_tags('<im<img>g src=x onerror=alert(1)>'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsIgnoresDataSrcAttribute(): void","+    {","+        $this->assertSame('real.gif', strip_image_tags('<img data-src=\"fake.gif\" src=\"real.gif\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('real.gif', strip_image_tags('<img src=\"real.gif\" data-src=\"fake.gif\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img data-src=\"fake.gif\">'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsWithoutSrcAttribute(): void","+    {","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img>'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<img alt=\"test\">'));","+        $this->assertSame('', strip_image_tags('<IMG ALT=\"test\">'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsIsCaseInsensitive(): void","+    {","+        $this->assertSame('photo.jpg', strip_image_tags('<IMG SRC=\"photo.jpg\">'));","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsFallbackWhenPcreFails(): void","+    {","+        $oldBacktrack = ini_get('pcre.backtrack_limit');","+        $oldJit       = ini_get('pcre.jit');","+","+        try {","+            // Force PCRE failure: JIT does not honour backtrack_limit.","+            ini_set('pcre.jit', '0');","+            ini_set('pcre.backtrack_limit', '1');","+","+            // Make sure PCRE really fails for this input, so the fallback is exercised.","+            // This also keeps the test independent of the test order: a pattern","+            // already compiled and JIT-cached by earlier tests still honours","+            // backtrack_limit once JIT is disabled, and the assertion below turns","+            // any silent PCRE success into an explicit failure.","+            $input  = '<img src=\"photo.jpg\" onerror=\"alert(1)\">';","+            $result = strip_image_tags($input);","+","+            $this->assertStringNotContainsString('<img', $result);","+            $this->assertStringContainsString('&lt;img', $result);","+","+            $result = strip_image_tags('Hello <img alt=\"a>b\" onerror=alert(1)> World');","+","+            $this->assertSame('Hello &lt;img alt=\"a>b\" onerror=alert(1)> World', $result);","+        } finally {","+            ini_set('pcre.backtrack_limit', (string) $oldBacktrack);","+            ini_set('pcre.jit', (string) $oldJit);","+        }","+    }","+","+    public function testStripImageTagsExceedingIterationLimitEscapesPrefix(): void","+    {","+        $input = str_repeat('<im', 26)","+            . '<img>'","+            . str_repeat('g>', 25)","+            . 'g src=x onerror=alert(1)>';","+","+        $output = strip_image_tags($input);","+","+        $this->assertStringNotContainsString('<img', $output);","+        $this->assertStringContainsString('&lt;img', $output);","     }"," ","     public function testEncodePhpTags(): void",""],"additions":116,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":186,"deletions":10,"truncated":false,"file_count":4},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-15T15:51:37.458260+00:00"}